<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    The trimming smoke sample. CI publishes it for linux-x64 as a self-contained, trimmed application with
    PublishTrimmed=true, TrimmerSingleWarn=false and SuppressTrimAnalysisWarnings=false, fails the job on a
    single "warning IL####" line in the publish log, and then runs the published binary. (The literal command
    lives in the trim-smoke job in .github/workflows/ci.yml; an XML comment cannot quote it, because it cannot
    contain a double hyphen.)

    PublishTrimmed, SelfContained and RuntimeIdentifier are therefore deliberately absent from this file: they
    belong to the publish job. Pinning a RID here would break the plain "dotnet run" against this project that
    the samples job, and any developer on Windows or macOS, performs.

    Single-target net10.0 on purpose. The publish passes no target framework and the job installs only the
    10.0.x SDK, so a multi-targeting project would fail immediately with the "project has multiple target
    frameworks" publish error. That single TFM is also why this project is not a member of EasyImageSharp.slnx:
    the test legs run against net8.0 as well, which fails for any solution project without a net8.0 build.

    InvariantGlobalization is deliberately NOT set. This job exists to catch trim warnings, and leaving
    globalization in the published closure keeps it closer to what a real consumer actually ships.

    Only EasyImageSharp is referenced. EasyImageSharp.AI must never be added: the ONNX Runtime managed wrapper
    is not annotated as AOT compatible, and its IL2026/IL3050 warnings would become publish errors under the
    TreatWarningsAsErrors inherited from the root Directory.Build.props.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <AssemblyName>Thumbnailer</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>Thumbnailer</RootNamespace>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\EasyImageSharp\EasyImageSharp.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
